ar is deeply  ingrained in these communities  and the government isn't doing any  messaging to combat it  we keep telling them that the hospital  health care system will not report them  their information is protected  then you meet the gentleman he will tell  you that he literally had to be  coaxed into going so he didn't go blind  we're calling him marcos because he  fears he may be deported if his identity  is revealed  his work as a cleaner is considered  essential he's been disinfecting and  cleaning buildings throughout the  pandemic  last year marcos came to paul's clinic  unable to see out of one eye  he was turned away by an ophthalmologist  because he was uninsured  paul recommended he go to emergency  suspecting that there was bleeding  inside of his eye  due to complications from his diabetes  when dr crawford said to you  you're going to have to go to the  hospital you're going to have to get  this procedure done  what did you say i say i don't  want to go marco says he's heard stories  of people going in for care  and having immigration authorities  called on them too many studies we  finally convinced him to go  and we gave him a letter i called the  hospital  emerged and said he's coming in he got  admitted but then he says the hospital  told him he would have to pay  paul stepped in again i guess you'd call  it advocacy or support  led to him getting the laser surgery i  just talked to him recently  i said how's your vision he said it's  getting much better he would have been  blind  when i asked marcos how he plans to get  the vaccine  he said he's waiting for paul's call  this cleaning for me  designed my life too is toronto public  health approved  and it's specifically for appropriate  vaccine storage  paul's on a mission to get vaccines to  his patients  he's trying to set up his own pop-up  vaccine clinic  there will be phone calls to thousands  of people  to say come in and give them a heads up  and the safety of the vaccine the  vaccine hesi